          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Collect four cards of the same rank and be quick to react to others' completion.",
          gameplay: 'All players sit in a circle with four cards each. Everyone simultaneously passes one card face down to the left and picks up the card from the right. There are no turns; passing continues as fast as players wish. You must pass one card before picking up the next; you may never hold more than four cards. When a player collects four of a kind they quietly touch their nose. As soon as one player touches their nose, all others may do the same. The last player to touch their nose loses the round (is the Pig).',
          keyRules: [
            'Pass one card at a time to your left; never hold more than four cards.',
            'First to collect four of a kind touches nose; others immediately do the same.',
            'Last to touch nose loses (the Pig).',
            'Play is simultaneous with no turns.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Don't blink! The cards are moving so fast that beginners often get 'Tunnel Vision' looking at their own hand. Your peripheral vision is your greatest assetâ€”watch the person directly across from you, not just your cards. If you see them freeze or reach for their face, react immediately even if you don't know who has the set.",
          intermediate: "The 'Slow Pass': If you have 3 cards of a rank, you only need one more. Stop passing quickly. Wait for the person to your right to drop a card. This allows you to focus 100% on other players' faces. If you rush the pass, you might miss the subtle finger-to-nose movement of the winner.",
          advanced: "The 'Fake-Out': If you are playing with veterans, try scratching your nose or adjusting your glasses. This often triggers a 'Panic Reaction' where everyone touches their noses. You get to laugh at them for being jumpy, and it masks your real win later in the round. Subtlety is the difference between a pro Pig player and a loser.",
          tips: [
            'If you are the one who completed the 4-of-a-kind, try to wait 2 or 3 seconds before touching your nose. Let the panic of the passing cards build first.',
            "If playing the 'Spoons' variation, grab the spoon softly. The sound of a clattering spoon ruins the surprise.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
